## Design Impact / health assessment

`/Users/normy/autobyteus_org/autobyteus-worktrees/context-compaction-simplification-analysis/tickets/in-progress/context-compaction-simplification-analysis/implementation-evidence/ir-004/design-impact-request.md` records source facts and executable reproducer.
The reviewed posture (Behavior Change + Refactor; ownership repair needed now)
is still correct, but its existing command-deduplication premise does not hold
for the actual Team/Org route. Standalone coordinator intercepts duplicate IDs;
Team/Org roots/configured handle do not. Fresh sequence therefore does not prove
fresh user intent there. Replaying identical B after recovery fails starts a
third compression operation and adds duplicate B, reproduced on both routes.

The current design supplies the intended outcome, but not the shared identity
boundary, lifetime, duplicate ACK/history or settled/rejected-command policy
needed across these owners. No guessed in-memory/durable ledger, duplicate queue,
standalone-readiness bypass or weaker retry policy is introduced. Return for a
proportionate technical decision; requirements need renewed approval only if
Solution Designer determines intended behavior must change.

